      "message": "Ok, after a lengthy discussion, this is definitely the macro-state of the VcnGatewayConnection. If you zoom out of the tunnel-specific connection state, this says \"should there be a tunnel\" or \"should their not\".\n\nWhat\u0027s weird is taht when the VcnGatewayConnection() is created, there is already at least one thing asking for a tunnel which means it\u0027s true at birth and false at death, and during its lifetime only changes from true to false one time.\n\nThus... after a length discussion, it\u0027s really a Kill-switch that causes the state machine to enter a terminal sequence, and the resulting decision is that it\u0027s more descriptive to change this from initially-true to initially-false, and rename it to:\n\nmIsQuitting or mIsExiting.... and the other controls around it should reference \"quit\" or \"exit\".",
